    "setup_id": "05601a00c6bc4954635863826740b7b61d18798ad2f99e32a9fef415a652990f",
    "text": "To determine the probability that each of Polya's next five stops is on the 7th floor or higher, we need to analyze the possible outcomes of her coin flips and their corresponding floor changes. Each flip of a fair coin can result in either heads (H) or tails (T), with each having a probability of \\( \\frac{1}{2} \\).\n\nPolya starts on the 6th floor. To end up on the 7th floor or higher after five coin flips, she needs to go up a total of at least 1 floor. This means she must have at least 3 heads (H) out of the 5 flips, because 3 heads will result in a net gain of 3 floors (from 6th to 7th, 8th, 9th, 10th, or 11th floor), and 2 heads and 3 tails will result in a net gain of 2 floors (from 6th to 7th or 8th floor), which is not sufficient.\n\nLet's calculate the number of favorable outcomes where she gets at least 3 heads in 5 flips. The number of ways to get exactly \\( k \\) heads in 5 flips is given by the binomial coefficient \\( \\binom{5}{k} \\).\n\nThe favorable outcomes are:\n- Getting exactly 3 heads: \\( \\binom{5}{3} = 10 \\)\n- Getting exactly 4 heads: \\( \\binom{5}{4} = 5 \\)\n- Getting exactly 5 heads: \\( \\binom{5}{5} = 1 \\)\n\nThe total number of favorable outcomes is:\n\\[\n\\binom{5}{3} + \\binom{5}{4} + \\binom{5}{5} = 10 + 5 + 1 = 16\n\\]\n\nThe total number of possible outcomes when flipping a coin 5 times is \\( 2^5 = 32 \\).\n\nTherefore, the probability that each of her next five stops is on the 7th floor or higher is:\n\\[\n\\frac{16}{32} = \\frac{1}{2}\n\\]\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{1}{2}}\n\\]",
    "timing_scope": "native prompt render, tokenize, transfer, CUDA-synchronized generate, decode; excludes loading/scoring",
